<section class="accordion-section section-width--thin">
  <h2 style="margin-bottom: 48px">[ Accordion - Component ]</h2>
  <p>
    Accordions can be used to tuck away lengthy info. They’re often used for FAQ
    sections. The
    <code>accordion.njk</code> component comes with the following configs:
  </p>
  <br />
  <br />

  <ul class="classic-list">
    <li>
      <code>id</code> a string, unique identifier if there’s more than one
      accordion
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>icon</code> an optional string, the path to the icon used for the
      accordion arrow. Default is an empty string (no icon)
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>plus</code> a boolean to use a plus sign (html markup) instad of an
      icon. Defaults to
      <code>false</code>
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>single_open</code> a boolean to only allow one accordion open at a
      time. Defaults to
      <code>false</code>
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>toggle_all</code> a boolean to show a button that opens or closes
      all accordion items at once. Requires <code>single_open</code> to be
      <code>false</code>. Defaults to <code>false</code>. Optionally override
      the button label via <code>toggle_all_text_open</code> and
      <code>toggle_all_text_close</code>, which default to
      <code>Open All</code> and <code>Close All</code>
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>items</code> an object that takes in <code>title</code> and
      <code>content</code> both of which are strings (content is 'safe' for
      markup) — used for the accordion title and message within. You also have
      access to <code>content_start</code> if using
      <code>skip-to-content</code> util in the header.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <br />
  <br />

  <p style="display: block; margin-bottom: 64px">
    Accordion with <code>icon</code> config and <code>single_open</code> set to
    true.
  </p>
  <!-- prettier-ignore -->
  {% set accordion = library.accordion.accordion_1 %}
  {% include '../_includes/components/accordion.njk' %}

  <br /><br /><br /><br />

  <p style="display: block; margin-bottom: 64px">
    Accordion with <code>plus</code> and <code>toggle_all</code> configs
  </p>
  <!-- prettier-ignore -->
  {% set accordion = library.accordion.accordion_2 %}
  {% include '../_includes/components/accordion.njk' %}
</section>

